of a finite field is cyclic; existence and uniqueness of $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}$ as the splitting field of $x^{p^n} - x$; the **relative algebraic closure** and **transitivity of algebraicity**; the **Frobenius endomorphism**; the **subfield lattice** of a finite field; and cyclicity of $\mathbb{F}_q^\times$ in general, not only for $q=p$.
